  "description": "SIKYAP crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C92 H124 Fe2 Gd4 N2 O30. From the CIF bond table, Fe1 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.203-3.619 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.46-106.60°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C92H124Fe2Gd4N2O30. Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
